  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Find $t$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e83,-1,7\u27e9,$ $b=\u27e8t,4,t\u27e9,$ and $c=\u27e82,6,8\u27e9$ are coplanar.",
  "worked_solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 7 \\\\ t & 4 & t \\\\ 2 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & t \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(4\\cdot 8-6\\cdot t)+(t\\cdot 8-2\\cdot t)+7(t\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =96-18t+8t-2t+42t-56 \\\\  & =30t+40 \\\\  & =10(3t+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10(3t+4) & =0 \\\\ 3t+4 & =0 \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-\\frac{4}{3}.$",
